Draw a clipped texture only where it is damaged (Omarchy Mobile)

renderTextureInternal() scissors a texture with a clip box or a clip region
(a surface's visible region from hyprland_surface_v1, which Quickshell sets
for a masked panel) to the clip alone, not to the clip within the damage, as
renderRect() and the other clipped paths do. Such a surface is redrawn whole
on every frame of anything on the screen: on a Pixel 7 Pro with the shell's
full-screen panels, an 8-pixel animation cost Hyprland 1.97 ms of fragment
work per frame (Panfrost's u_trace), as much as a full-screen change.

--- a/src/render/OpenGL.cpp
+++ b/src/render/OpenGL.cpp
@@ -1581,6 +1581,11 @@
                 damageClip.intersect(data.clipRegion);
         }
 
+        // Only the damage within the clip, as without one: a surface with a
+        // visible region (hyprland_surface_v1, a Quickshell panel's mask) was
+        // redrawn whole on every frame of anything on the screen.
+        damageClip.intersect(*data.damage);
+
         if (!damageClip.empty()) {
             damageClip.forEachRect([this](const auto& RECT) {
                 scissor(&RECT, g_pHyprRenderer->m_renderData.transformDamage);
